	//   x = 0.345702914918791, y = 0.3585385966799326, Y = 1.0
	// Table layout for a 3-in/3-out CLUT with n grid points, index of output channel c
	// at grid node (i0, i1, i2):  ((i0 * n + i1) * n + i2) * 3 + c   -- input channel 2 varies fastest.
	// Every case passes Bright = 0.0 to the C function; brightness enters only as
	// gammaL = pow(10, -Bright / 100) with gammaA = gammaB = 1.0.
	// Rgb8OutHex is the sRGB -> abstract -> sRGB TYPE_RGB_8 result for Rgb8Probes (125 pixels).
	// TableLength is GridPoints^3 * 3 (the number of 16-bit CLUT entries). TableSha256 covers the
	// whole table serialised as little-endian ushorts; TableSamples is a ~200-entry evenly spaced
	// slice for tolerance-based comparison: TableSamples[i] == table[i * TableSampleStride].

